// A fixed-size array cannot be the direct element of a Vec: a C array is not an
// assignable value, so the container could never copy elements into its buffer.
// This must be rejected at sema with a clear diagnostic rather than silently
// emitting invalid C (an undefined element typedef and an array assignment).
// The fix is to wrap the array in a data type, or use a nested Vec.
unit main() {
  Vec<[3]int> rows = [];
  rows.push([1, 2, 3]);
  log(rows.len as int);
}
